hadiths[96]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3761","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\The oath by which the Messenger of Allah used to swear was: 'No"
"3762","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet said:\\""Whoever swears an oath and says: 'If Allah wills'"""
"3763","It was narrated from 'Umar bin Al-Khattab that the Prophet said:\\""Actions are but by intentions"""
"3764","Ubaid bin 'Umair said:I heard 'Aishah say: \\""The Prophet used to stay with Zainab bint Jahsh and drink honey at her house. Hafsah and I agreed that if the Prophet came to either of us"""
"3765","It was narrated that Jabir said:\\""I entered the house of the Prophet with him and there was some bread and vinegar. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Eat; what a good condiment is vinegar"""
"3766","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:\\""At the time of the Messenger of Allah we used to be called Samasir (brokers). The Messenger of Allah came to us when we were selling and called us by a name that was better than that. He said: 'O merchants (Tujjar)"""
"3767","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:\\""We used to sell in Al-Baqi"""
"3768","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:\\""The Prophet came to us when we were in the marketplace and said: 'This marketplace is filled with idle talk and (false) oaths"""
"3769","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:\\""In Al-Madinah we used to buy and sell Wasqs (of goods)"""
"3770","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah forbade vows and said:\\""They do not bring any good; they are just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"""
"3771","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah forbade vows and said: 'They do not change anything; they are just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"""
"3772","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'A vow does not bring anything forward or put it back; it is just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"""
"3773","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""A vow does not bring anything to the son of Adam that has not been decreed for him. It is just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"""
"3774","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:\\""Do not make vows"""
"3775","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Whoever vows to obey Allah"""
"3776","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'Whoever vows to obey Allah"""
"3777","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'Whoever vows to obey Allah"""
"3778","Imran bin Husain said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The best of you are my generation"""
"3779","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah passed by a man who was leading another man by a rope. The Prophet took it"""
"3780","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas:\\""The Prophet passed by a man who was circumambulating the Ka'bah"""
"3781","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that the Prophet said:\\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3782","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Messenger of Allah said:\If any one of you swears an oath"
"3783","It was narrated that 'Uqbah bin 'Amir said:\\""My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah"""
"3784","Uqbah bin 'Amir narrated that he asked the Prophet about a sister of his who had vowed to walk"
"3785","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""A woman traveled by sea and vowed to fast for a month"""
"3786","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah about a vow which his mother had sworn"
"3787","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah about a vow which his mother had sworn"""
"3788","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\\""Sa'd bin 'Ubadah came to the Prophet and said: 'My mother died and she had sworn a vow"""
"3789","It was narrated that 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah said:\The Prophet said to me: 'If you swear an oath"
"3790","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""Umar had made a vow to spend a night in 'Itikaf in Al-Masjid Al-Haram. He asked the Messenger of Allah about that"""
"3791","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that 'Umar had vowed -during the Jahiliyyah- to spend a day in 'Itikaf. He asked the Messenger of Allah about that"
"3792","'Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah said:\There is no vow and no oath concerning that which one does not possess"
"3793","Abdur-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik narrated that 'Abdullah bin Ka'b said:\\""I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his Hadith about when he stayed behind and did not join the Messenger of Allah on the campaign to Tabuk. He said: 'When I sat down before him I said: \""\""O Messenger of Allah"""
"3794","Abdullah bin Ka'b bin Malik said:\\""I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his Hadith about when he stayed behind and did not join the Messenger of Allah on the campaign to Tabuk. (he said) I said: 'As part of my repentance I want to give my wealth in charity for Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Keep some of your wealth for yourself; that is better for you.' I said: 'I will keep for myself my share that is in Khaibar"""
"3795","It was narrated from 'Ubaydullah bin Ka'b:\\""I heard my father Ka'b bin Malik narrate: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah"""
"3796","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""We were with the Messenger of Allah in the year of Khaibar"""
"3797","Abdullah bin 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills"""
"3798","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills"""
"3799","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Whoever swears an oath and says"""
"3800","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""Sulaiman bin Dawud said: 'Tonight I will go around ninety women"""
"3801","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin 'Amir that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""The expiation for vows is the expiation for an oath"""
"3802","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3803","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath"""
"3804","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3805","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3806","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3807","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3808","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3809","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"""
"3810","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\The Messenger of Allah passed by a man who was leading another man by a rope. The Prophet took it"
"3811","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath"""
"3812","It was narrated that 'Imran said:The Messenger of Allah said: \\""There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath"""
"3813","It was narrated that 'Imran said:The Messenger of Allah said: \\""There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.\""\"" It was said: \""\""Az-Zubair did not hear this Hadith from 'Imran bin Husain"""
"3814","It was narrated that 'Uqbah bin 'Amir said:\My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah"
"3815","It was narrated that Muhammad bin Az-Zubayr Hanzali said:My father told me that a man told him"
"3816","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: \\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or at the time of anger"""
"3817","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: \\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.\""\"" Mansur bin Zadhan contradicted him in his wording"""
"3818","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: \\""There is no vow for the son of Adam with regard to that which he does not possess"""
"3819","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Prophet said:\\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess"""
"3820","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: \\""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess"""
"3821","It was narrated that Anas said:\\""The Prophet saw a man being supported by two others and said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He vowed to walk to the House of Allah.' He said: 'Allah has no need for this man to torture himself. Tell him to ride"""
"3822","It was narrated that Anas said:\\""The Messenger of Allah passed by an old man who was being supported between two men and said: 'What is the matter with him?' They said: 'He vowed to walk.' He said: 'Allah has no need for him to torture himself. Tell him to ride.'\""\"" So he was told to ride"""
"3823","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:\\""The Messenger of Allah came to a man who was being supported by two others and said: 'What is the matter with him?' It was said: 'He vowed to walk to the Ka'bah.' He said: 'Allah does not benefit from his torturing himself.' And he told him to ride"""
"3824","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\\""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: \""\""If Allah wills"""
"3825","Abdullah bin Ka'b bin Malik said:""I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his Hadith about when he stayed behind and did not join the Messenger of Allah on the campaign to Tabuk. (he said) I said: 'As part of my repentance I want to give my wealth in charity for Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Keep some of your wealth for yourself; that is better for you.' I said: 'I will keep for myself my share that is in Khaibar"
"3826","It was narrated from 'Ubaydullah bin Ka'b:n I heard my father Ka'b bin Malik narrate: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has saved me by my being truthful, and as part of my repentance I want to give my wealth in charity to Allah and His Messenger. He said: Keep some of your wealth for yourself; that is better for you. I said: I will keep my share that is in Khaibar.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3857 Arabic Hadees: 3857"
"3827","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:n We were with the Messenger of Allah in the year of Khaibar, and we did not get any spoils of war except for wealth, goods and clothes. Then a man from Banu Ad-Dubaib, who was called Rifa'ah bin Zaid, gave the Messenger of Allah a black slave who was called Mid'am. The Messenger of Allah set out for Wadi Al-Qura. When we were in Wadi Al-Qura, while Mid'am was unloading the luggage of the Messenger of Allah, an arrow came and killed him. The people said: 'Congratulations! You will go to Paradise,' but the Messenger of Allah said: 'No, by the One in Whose hand is my soul! The cloak that he took from the spoils of war on the Day of Khaibar is burning him with fire.' When the people heard that, a man brought one or two shoelaces to the Messenger of Allah and the Messenger of Allah said: 'One or two shoelaces of fire.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3858 Arabic Hadees: 3858"
"3828","Abdullah bin 'Umar said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, then he has made an exception.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3859 Arabic Hadees: 3859"
"3829","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, then he has made an exception.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3860 Arabic Hadees: 3860"
"3830","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:n Whoever swears an oath and says, 'If Allah wills,' then he has the choice: If he wishes, he may go ahead, and if he wishes he may not. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3861 Arabic Hadees: 3861"
"3831","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:n Sulaiman bin Dawud said: 'Tonight I will go around ninety women, each of whom will bear a horseman who will perform Jihad in the cause of Allah.' His companion said to him: 'If Allah wills.' But he did not say: 'If Allah wills.' Then he went around to them all, but none of them got pregnant except a woman who bore half a man. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! If he had said, 'If Allah wills,' they would all have performed Jihad in the cause of Allah as horsemen. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3862 Arabic Hadees: 3862"
"3832","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin 'Amir that the Messenger of Allah said:n The expiation for vows is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3863 Arabic Hadees: 3863"
"3833","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3864 Arabic Hadees: 3864"
"3834","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3865 Arabic Hadees: 3865"
"3835","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3866 Arabic Hadees: 3866"
"3836","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3867 Arabic Hadees: 3867"
"3837","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3868 Arabic Hadees: 3868"
"3838","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3869 Arabic Hadees: 3869"
"3839","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3870 Arabic Hadees: 3870"
"3840","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3871 Arabic Hadees: 3871"
"3841","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain, may Allah be pleased with him, said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3872 Arabic Hadees: 3872"
"3842","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3873 Arabic Hadees: 3873"
"3843","It was narrated that 'Imran said:nThe Messenger of Allah said: There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3874 Arabic Hadees: 3874"
"3844","It was narrated that 'Imran said:nThe Messenger of Allah said: There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. It was said: Az-Zubair did not hear this Hadith from 'Imran bin Husain. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3875 Arabic Hadees: 3875"
"3845","It was narrated from Muhammad bin Az-Zubair, from his father, from a man from the inhabitants of Al-Basrah, who said:n I accompanied 'Imran bin Husain, who said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Vows are of two types: A vow that is made to do an act of obedience to Allah; that is for Allah and must be fulfilled, and a vow that is made to do an act of disobedience to Allah; that is for Shaitan and should not be fulfilled, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3876 Arabic Hadees: 3876"
"3846","It was narrated that Muhammad bin Az-Zubayr Hanzali said:nMy father told me that a man told him, that he asked 'Imran bin Husain about a man who made a vow not to attend the prayers in the mosque of his people. 'Imran said: I heard the Messenger of Allah say: There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3877 Arabic Hadees: 3877"
"3847","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:nThe Messenger of Allah said: There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or at the time of anger, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3878 Arabic Hadees: 3878"
"3848","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:nThe Messenger of Allah said: There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. Mansur bin Zadhan contradicted him in his wording. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3879 Arabic Hadees: 3879"
"3849","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:nThe Messenger of Allah said: There is no vow for the son of Adam with regard to that which he does not possess, or to do an act of disobedience to Allah, the Mighty and Sublime. 'Ali bin Zaid contradicted him -for he reported it from Al-Hasan from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3880 Arabic Hadees: 3880"
"3850","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Prophet said:n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3881 Arabic Hadees: 3881"
"3851","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:nThe Messenger of Allah said: There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3882 Arabic Hadees: 3882"
"3852","It was narrated that Anas said:n The Prophet saw a man being supported by two others and said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He vowed to walk to the House of Allah.' He said: 'Allah has no need for this man to torture himself. Tell him to ride.' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3883 Arabic Hadees: 3883"
"3853","It was narrated that Anas said:n The Messenger of Allah passed by an old man who was being supported between two men and said: 'What is the matter with him?' They said: 'He vowed to walk.' He said: 'Allah has no need for him to torture himself. Tell him to ride.' So he was told to ride. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3884 Arabic Hadees: 3884"
"3854","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:n The Messenger of Allah came to a man who was being supported by two others and said: 'What is the matter with him?' It was said: 'He vowed to walk to the Ka'bah.' He said: 'Allah does not benefit from his torturing himself.' And he told him to ride. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3885 Arabic Hadees: 3885"
"3855","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:n The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, then he has made an exception. ' nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3886 Arabic Hadees: 3886"
"3856","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, who attributed it to the Prophet:n Sulaiman said: 'I will certainly go around to ninety women tonight, each of whom will bear a child who will fight in the cause of Allah.' It was said to him: 'Say: If Allah wills' but he did not say it. He went around to them but none of them bore a child except for one woman who bore half a person. The Messenger of Allah said: If he had said: 'If Allah wills,' he would not have broken his vow, and this would have been a means to help him to get what he wanted. nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3887 Arabic Hadees: 3887"
